      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZR.2.59",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZR.2.59",
      "verse": 59,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they who went up from Tel-melah, Tel-harsa, Cherub, Addan, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Immer: but they could not show their fathers' house, and their seed, whether they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of Israel:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZR.2.60",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZR.2.60",
      "verse": 60,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The children of Delaiah, the children of Tobiah, the children of Nekoda, six hundred fifty and two.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZR.2.61",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZR.2.61",
      "verse": 61,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And of the children of the priests: the children of Habaiah, the children of Koz, the children of Barzillai: who took a wife of the daughters of Barzillai the Gileadite, and was called after their name:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZR.2.62",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZR.2.62",
      "verse": 62,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "These sought their register ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "among",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " those that were reckoned by genealogy, but they were not found: therefore were they, as polluted, put from the priesthood.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZR.2.63",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZR.2.63",
      "verse": 63,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the Tirshatha said to them, that they should not eat of the most holy things, till there stood up a priest with Urim and with Thummim.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
